    "question_id": "q03",
    "platform": "Claude",
    "answer": "Sum 1..100 = 5050.\nMultiples of 3: 3·(33·34/2)=3·561=1683.\nMultiples of 5: 5·(20·21/2)=5·210=1050.\nMultiples of 15: 15·(6·7/2)=15·21=315.\n\n5050 − 1683 − 1050 + 315 = 2632\n\n2632",
    "recorded_at": "2026-11-17T22:25:02.732Z"
  },
  {
    "question_id": "q03",
    "platform": "DeepSeek",
    "answer": "5050 - (sum of multiples of 3) - (sum of multiples of 5) + (sum of multiples of 15)\n\nSum 1..100 = 5050\nMultiples of 3: 3+6+...+99 = 3(1+...+33) = 3561 = 1683\nMultiples of 5: 5+10+...+100 = 5(1+...+20) = 5210 = 1050\nMultiples of 15: 15+30+...+90 = 15(1+...+6) = 1521 = 315\n\n5050 - 1683 - 1050 + 315 = 2632\n\n2632",
    "recorded_at": "2026-11-17T22:25:02.732Z"
  },
  {
    "question_id": "q04",
    "platform": "Claude",
    "answer": "Compute 7^103 mod 13. Since 13 is prime, 7^12 ≡ 1 (mod 13), so reduce the exponent: 103 mod 12 = 7 (103 = 8·12 + 7). That leaves 7^7 mod 13.\n\n7^2 = 49 ≡ 10\n7^4 ≡ 10^2 = 100 ≡ 9\n7^6 ≡ 9 · 10 = 90 ≡ 12\n7^7 ≡ 12 · 7 = 84 ≡ 6 (since 84 = 78 + 6)\n\n6",
    "recorded_at": "2026-11-17T22:25:45.240Z"
