    "platform": "Claude",
    "answer": "Treat C and D as a single block, which can be ordered 2 ways internally (CD or DE... i.e., CD or DC).\n\nThat leaves 4 units to arrange: A, B, E, and the block. There are 4! = 24 arrangements of these units.\n\nA comes before B in exactly half of them, so 12.\n\nMultiplying by the 2 internal orderings of the block gives 12 × 2 = 24.\n\n24",
